WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.010
Two rival firms make a secret deal:

2
00:00:03.010 --> 00:00:05.750
each will produce just 20 units.

3
00:00:05.750 --> 00:00:07.270
If both keep the deal,

4
00:00:07.270 --> 00:00:09.560
each earns a profit of 800.

5
00:00:09.560 --> 00:00:12.820
But each firm could quietly produce more.

6
00:00:12.820 --> 00:00:15.740
And no court will
enforce a deal like this.

7
00:00:15.740 --> 00:00:19.260
So what happens when each firm
makes its own best choice?

8
00:00:19.260 --> 00:00:21.390
Could both end up worse off?

9
00:00:21.390 --> 00:00:24.690
In this mission, you'll find
each firm's dominant strategy

10
00:00:24.690 --> 00:00:26.290
in a payoff matrix.

11
00:00:26.290 --> 00:00:28.780
Then you'll set a penalty in a graph lab,

12
00:00:28.780 --> 00:00:32.240
and predict when keeping the
deal becomes the best choice.

13
00:00:32.240 --> 00:00:35.670
Your mission: find out how
two sensible choices can

14
00:00:35.670 --> 00:00:37.490
leave both firms with less.
